<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Australia's MBIA notes assigned Aaa rating.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Australia's MBIA notes assigned Aaa rating.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ratings agency Moody's Investor Service said on Wednesday it had assigned a Aaa rating to the A$88.7 million of medium term notes issued as MBIA Series 1 by Australia's Prime Asset Vehicle (No 2) Ltd.</p>
<p>&quot;The issuer will use the proceeds of the MBIA Series 1 notes to refinance the acquisition and holding of two hospitals owned by companies within the Ramsay Health Care Group,&quot; Moody's said.</p>
<p>Prime Asset Vehicle is managed by County NatWest Corporate Finance.</p>
<p>The notes are fully amortising floating rate notes with a 2005 maturity.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 373-1800</p>
</text>
